<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tatar ASSR</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a>–<a href="/years/1990">1990</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tatar Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic was an autonomous republic within the Russian Soviet Federative Socialist Republic, created in May 1920 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazan">Kazan</a> as its capital. It replaced earlier plans for a larger Tatar-Bashkir state and covered only part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> Tatar population. In 1990 it declared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> and became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatarstan">Republic of Tatarstan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tatar-assr.jpg" alt="Tatar ASSR" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osipov Georgy Nokka · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Tatar_ASSR.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
